  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 129 PM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nThe upper level flow will remain out of the west-northwest through \nmuch of next week, allowing a series of shortwaves to sweep though \nour region. The low level boundary will reside across our area early \nin the week, which will keep a more favorable environment in place \nfor severe storms through Tuesday. LREF guidance has the highest \nprobability (40-50%) of surface CAPE exceeding 2000 j/kg along with \nat least 35 kts of effective shear across our north on Monday before \nnudging it south on Tuesday. The boundary likely slips to our south \nby Wednesday and beyond, but remains close enough to keep daily \nshower and thunderstorm chances in place as additional upper level \nwaves move across. The GFS appears to be an outlier at this time, \ndepicting dry surface high pressure taking control of our weather by \nnext Fri/Sat. Ensemble guidance generally keeps the wetter pattern \nin place. The LREF probability of receiving at least 2\" through next \nSaturday is around 35-45% across our region.\n\nTemperatures start off the week on the hot side, ranging from the \nmid 80s to around 90. High humidity levels will also be in place, \nwhich may allow heat index readings to exceed 100 on Monday and \npossibly again on Tuesday (which may require additional heat \nheadlines). Much cooler temperatures are expected during the latter \npart of the week with the LREF suggesting a 60-90% chance highs \nremain below 80 by Thursday along and north of I-80 and the entire \narea by next Fri-Sat.",
